From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a hidden webview keeps its page's viewport

A <webview> under `display: none` has no layout object, and
RemoteFrameView::UpdateCompositingRect set its compositing rect to
empty. That rect is the page's compositor viewport, so a hidden page's
viewport went to 0x0. cc then threw away the tiles patch 0252 keeps for
a hidden page, and showing the page again rastered its whole viewport.

manganese hides the windows of other workspaces this way. A lyra trace
of workspace switches on battery shows the arriving claude.ai page
rastering about 400 tiles before its first frame on every switch, with
the GPU process busy for the whole slide.

- A <webview> with no layout object keeps the compositing rect it had.
- Its frame rect, visibility and every other frame's rect are as
  before.

Guarded by `guard-webview-reshown-tiles.sh`, which now fails when the
page's compositor viewport goes to 0x0 (the pinned engine: once per
hide).

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on crux.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011frZaqdnEUiniYFYDxHzpg
---
 .../blink/renderer/core/frame/remote_frame_view.cc   | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/remote_frame_view.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/remote_frame_view.cc
index 251d6dc..cce00db 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/remote_frame_view.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/remote_frame_view.cc
@@ -272,10 +272,20 @@ gfx::Rect RemoteFrameView::ComputeCompositingRect() const {
 void RemoteFrameView::UpdateCompositingRect() {
   remote_frame_->UpdateCompositedLayerBounds();
   gfx::Rect previous_rect = compositing_rect_;
-  compositing_rect_ = gfx::Rect();
   LocalFrameView* local_root_view = ParentLocalRootFrameView();
   LayoutEmbeddedContent* owner_layout_object =
       remote_frame_->OwnerLayoutObject();
+  // Domicile: a <webview> with no layout object, as under `display: none`,
+  // keeps its compositing rect. The rect is its page's compositor viewport
+  // (RemoteFrame::SynchronizeVisualProperties), and an empty one throws away
+  // the tiles a hidden page keeps (patch 0252). Shells hide the windows of
+  // other workspaces this way, and an empty rect would make every workspace
+  // switch raster the arriving page in the middle of its slide.
+  if (!owner_layout_object &&
+      IsA<HTMLWebViewElement>(remote_frame_->DeprecatedLocalOwner())) {
+    return;
+  }
+  compositing_rect_ = gfx::Rect();
   if (!local_root_view || !owner_layout_object) {
     SetNeedsFrameRectPropagation();
     return;
